;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljs:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved.
;;
;; FIVE independent authorities are cited, not one:
;;   * GLEIF, the global LEI system (the entity record, the RA000412 entry in the
;;     registration-authorities registry, the T417 entry in the entity-legal-forms
;;     registry, and the LEI record of the managing LOU)
;;   * Japan's National Tax Agency, at the corporate-number publication site
;;     (houjin-bangou.nta.go.jp) under corporate number 7010001065142
;;   * Japan's METI, at gBizINFO (info.gbiz.go.jp) under the same corporate number
;;   * the United States, via the SEC's EDGAR submissions API (the former
;;     NYSE-listed ADR filer, CIK 0000769594 -- 20-F, 6-K, F-6 POS, 25, 15F-12B)
;;   * the issuer itself, at the Social Media Policy page this repository archives
;;     and at its published inquiry form
;;
;; HOW THE JAPANESE STATE AND GLEIF ARE LINKED -- BY SHARED KEY. GLEIF names
;; RA000412 -- Companies Registration (登記) at the Legal Affairs Bureau (法務局)
;; -- as both register of record and validation authority, and records
;; registeredAs 0100-01-065142 (the 会社法人等番号, the commercial-registry
;; number). Japan's corporate number (法人番号) is BY CONSTRUCTION one check
;; digit prefixed to those same 12 digits: 7 + 010001065142 = 7010001065142.
;; The NTA and gBizINFO rows below resolve THAT number to this legal name at
;; this seat. So the GLEIF<->Japan link is a direct key, not an address match.
;; The NTA designated the number on 平成27年10月5日 (2015-10-05, row
;; nta-designation-date).
;;
;; THE RENAME, RECORDED BY TWO STATES. Effective 令和7年7月1日 (2025-07-01) the
;; entity changed its trade name from 日本電信電話株式会社 (Nippon Telegraph and
;; Telephone Corporation) to ＮＴＴ株式会社 (NTT, Inc.). GLEIF carries the old
;; name as PREVIOUS_LEGAL_NAME (row gleif-previous-name); the NTA change history
;; carries the event 商号又は名称の変更 with that 事由発生年月日 (rows
;; nta-previous-name, nta-rename-event, nta-rename-effective). The SEC has NOT
;; recorded the rename: EDGAR still prints the former English name (row
;; sec-former-name), because the filer went dormant in 2018 after Form 25 /
;; 15F-12B ADR deregistration (last filing 2018-04-13; the ADR now trades OTC
;; as NTTYY, row sec-adr-ticker). So the GLEIF<->SEC link is by FORMER name +
;; address only -- EDGAR also carries "lei":null (row sec-lei-null, which goes
;; red the day EDGAR starts printing the LEI, at which point a direct-key row
;; should replace it).
;;
;; THE ADDRESS TRIANGLE. GLEIF records 大手町一丁目5番1号, 東京都 千代田区,
;; postal 100-8116 (rows gleif-address, gleif-city, gleif-postal). The SEC's own
;; address record prints OTEMACHI FIRST SQUARE, EAST TOWER, 5-1, OTEMACHI
;; 1-CHOME, CHIYODA-KU, TOKYO JAPAN, 100-8116 (rows sec-street, sec-street2,
;; sec-city, sec-zip). The NTA and gBizINFO print 東京都千代田区大手町１丁目５番１号
;; (rows nta-address, gbiz-address). Three states' worth of registers, one seat,
;; none of them quoting each other.
;;
;; WHY THE REGISTER OF RECORD HAS NO PER-ENTITY ROW. The Legal Affairs Bureau's
;; registry is served through the paid, login-gated 登記情報提供サービス at
;; www1.touki.or.jp (the very website GLEIF's RA000412 entry names). The portal
;; answers HTTP 200 (row touki-portal) but exposes no stable public per-entity
;; URL, so no row can cite the registry extract itself. The registry NUMBER is
;; instead corroborated through the NTA corporate number, which embeds it (see
;; the shared-key paragraph above).
;;
;; WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT CITED. GLEIF's nextRenewalDate moves every year by
;; construction; a row on it would go red on schedule while saying nothing
;; about the entity. The TSE ticker 9432 (claimed in blueprint.edn and
;; README.md) has no server-rendered per-entity page at jpx.co.jp that this
;; gate could check, so it is NOT proven by any row here -- row sec-adr-ticker
;; proves only that EDGAR lists the OTC ADR ticker NTTYY, and the managing-LOU
;; rows prove only that the LOU is Tokyo Stock Exchange, Inc., not that this
;; entity lists there. The former corporate site www.ntt.co.jp answers HTTP 410
;; Gone (noted in README.md); no row cites it -- the issuer rows cite the
;; current group site group.ntt, including the exact page whose text
;; 80-data/public/tos.journal.edn archives (:tos/source-url
;; https://group.ntt/en/privacy/social.html, still live -- row
;; issuer-social-policy). The EDGAR body also carries a filings list that
;; changed with every filing while the filer was active; rows target only
;; stable header fields.
;;
;; :cite/row-kind is the honest part of this catalog and should be read before
;; the claims:
;;
;;   :identity   the substring names this entity, its identifiers, or its seat.
;;               Point the URL at a different company and the row fails.
;;   :attribute  the substring is TRUE OF THIS ENTITY BUT NOT ONLY OF IT
;;               (status ACTIVE, city TOKYO, a Reiwa date, an SIC code).
;;               Such a row can survive a swap to a similar company. It is
;;               recorded because it corroborates, not because it identifies.
;;   :definition the substring resolves a code or body the entity record points
;;               at (RA000412, T417, the managing LOU, the registry portal). It
;;               says the named register, legal form or LOU exists; it says
;;               nothing about NTT by itself.
;;
;; Of the entries below, 17 are :identity, 19 are :attribute and 5 are
;; :definition. A reader who treats all 41 as identifying would overstate what
;; this catalog proves -- which is the error this field exists to prevent.
;;
;; Substrings are taken from the RAW response body (GLEIF JSON escapes Japanese
;; text as \uXXXX, so GLEIF rows over Japanese values pin the literal
;; backslash-u bytes; the NTA, gBizINFO and issuer HTML serve UTF-8 and are
;; pinned in Japanese; EDGAR JSON is ASCII) and were each checked against the
;; fetched bytes before this file was written (2026-08-22).
